  comment on table "playon"."main_marts_data"."dim_user" is $dbt_comment_literal_block$**Grain: one row per registered account.** 8,000 rows. The conformed user dimension.
Attributes only — no engagement measures, which live in `product/fct_user_engagement`. Keeping the Product team's engagement definition out of the dimension is precisely what lets the Data team adopt this table without inheriting our definition.
Subscription state is included as flags and counts, because "what plan is this person on" is an attribute of the person. Expressed as scalars rather than an array of subscription ids: arrays are hostile to most BI tools and this dimension is meant to be reused beyond the Product team. Anyone needing the enumeration joins `dim_subscription_history`.
$dbt_comment_literal_block$;

  
