  comment on table "playon"."main_marts_data"."fct_user_paid_spells" is $dbt_comment_literal_block$**Grain: one row per continuous period during which a user was a paying customer.** 3,197 rows, merged from 4,277 paid windows.
A factless fact — it records a timespan rather than a measure. Exists because 319 overlapping subscription pairs across 268 users involve two *paid* plans, which makes "was this person paying on date X" ambiguous at subscription grain. Worse, a user who cancels one of two concurrent subscriptions looks churned while still paying; counting subscription cancellations as churn would overstate it for exactly those users. **859 spells absorb more than one window**, so the problem is real, not theoretical.
