  comment on view "playon"."main_staging"."stg_asset_catalog" is $dbt_comment_literal_block$**Grain: one row per distinct video asset.** 862 rows.
The source `asset_id` is not unique -- 12 ids cover 24 rows, each pair being a game and its "(Replay)". These are two real assets sharing one id, so `asset_key` (a surrogate over asset_id + title + asset_type) is the true key and `asset_id` is retained as the natural key for joining to telemetry.
**Known limitation:** playback events carry only `asset_id`, so events on those 12 ids cannot be attributed to the live broadcast versus the replay. The surrogate key fixes the dimension's grain; it cannot recover information the fact table never captured.
**This model is also the published catalog dimension.** A thin `dim_asset_catalog` passthrough was deleted in WP-005 -- it added one derived column and hid three lineage columns, which is not enough work to justify a model, and keeping it would have been the same cargo-cult layering criticised in `models/intermediate/README.md`. Staging is Data-owned and published in this project, so consuming it directly is coherent. Use it for catalog reporting -- what exists, by sport, type and school. For anything joined to viewing, use `dim_asset`, which is the join-safe grain.
$dbt_comment_literal_block$;

  
