  comment on table "playon"."main_marts_product"."fct_session_engagement" is $dbt_comment_literal_block$**Grain: one row per viewing session.** 5,739 rows. The model that carries the Product team's opinion, and deliberately nothing else.
It takes the factual `completion_pct` from `data/fct_session` and applies a threshold. That is its entire contribution — and its entire reason for existing as a separate model. An earlier version applied the threshold inside the session model itself, which would have forced any team adopting sessionization to inherit our 30% cut whether they agreed or not.
**The definition:** an engaged view is a session in which the viewer watched at least 30% of the asset's runtime. 1,826 of 5,739 sessions (31.8%) qualify.
**Why 30% is not arbitrary:** it is the midpoint of an *empty band* in the observed completion distribution (0.200 → 0.478). Every threshold in that band classifies all 5,739 sessions identically, so nothing depends on the precise value — and the knob cannot be quietly tuned toward a retention result. Full reasoning in `dev_docs/domain/engaged-view.md` §5.2 and §6.
$dbt_comment_literal_block$;

  
